WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.518
For over a month, the travelers stayed at Squire Kou's house.

2
00:00:07.519 --> 00:00:15.062
Every time they tried to leave, the squire begged them to stay longer.

3
00:00:15.063 --> 00:00:21.230
Finally, one morning during breakfast, the Tang Monk insisted on leaving.

4
00:00:21.231 --> 00:00:25.086
"We'll never fetch the True Scriptures if we stay here."

5
00:00:25.087 --> 00:00:28.430
"Please don't leave," said Squire Kou.

6
00:00:28.431 --> 00:00:30.812
[g@"You are very important monks.

7
00:00:30.813 --> 00:00:33.759
Having you as guests is a good deed."@g]

8
00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:36.976
[g@"I'd like to stay here," said Bajie.

9
00:00:36.977 --> 00:00:39.837
He took a bite of a peach.@g]

10
00:00:39.838 --> 00:00:43.055
[g@"No. Master's right," said Wukong.

11
00:00:43.056 --> 00:00:45.682
"We must continue our journey."@g]

12
00:00:45.683 --> 00:00:47.997
[g@Lady Kou grew angry.

13
00:00:47.998 --> 00:00:51.027
"You monks are ungrateful!@g]

14
00:00:51.028 --> 00:00:54.148
[g@We have fed you and taken care of you.

15
00:00:54.149 --> 00:00:56.899
Yet you can't wait to leave!"@g]

16
00:00:56.900 --> 00:01:00.645
[g@"We are very grateful," said the Tang Monk.

17
00:01:00.646 --> 00:01:04.599
"But we cannot stay any longer."@g]

18
00:01:04.600 --> 00:01:09.407
After breakfast Wujing got the horse from Squire Kou's stable.

19
00:01:09.408 --> 00:01:11.557
Bajie gathered the bags.

20
00:01:11.558 --> 00:01:21.260
The Tang Monk thanked Squire and Lady Kou, and the travelers headed west.

21
00:01:21.261 --> 00:01:28.898
"They are ungrateful," muttered Lady Kou.

22
00:01:28.899 --> 00:01:33.689
The next morning Lady Kou ran into the town's courthouse.

23
00:01:33.690 --> 00:01:36.542
[g@Tears filled her eyes.

24
00:01:36.543 --> 00:01:41.046
"I must speak with the judge!" she cried.@g]

25
00:01:41.047 --> 00:01:43.202
[g@The judge rushed to her.

26
00:01:43.203 --> 00:01:45.970
"Lady Kou! What's wrong?"@g]

27
00:01:45.971 --> 00:01:51.572
"Robbers broke into our house last night," said Lady Kou breathlessly.

28
00:01:51.573 --> 00:01:56.021
"They stole many valuable items and two of our horses.

29
00:01:56.022 --> 00:02:00.689
Squire Kou tried to stop them, but the robbers . . .

30
00:02:00.690 --> 00:02:06.052
[g@They . . . killed my husband!"

31
00:02:06.053 --> 00:02:08.716
Lady Kou burst into tears.@g]

32
00:02:08.717 --> 00:02:10.507
[g@The judge gasped.

33
00:02:10.508 --> 00:02:13.910
"Oh no! Did you see the robbers?"@g]

34
00:02:13.911 --> 00:02:15.970
[g@Lady Kou sniffed.

35
00:02:15.971 --> 00:02:19.775
"Yes, and I know who they are."@g]

36
00:02:19.776 --> 00:02:22.302
"Who are they?" asked the judge.

37
00:02:22.303 --> 00:02:24.713
[g@Lady Kou gritted her teeth.

38
00:02:24.714 --> 00:02:29.799
"The Tang Monk and his companions!"@g]

39
00:02:29.800 --> 00:02:32.319
The judge turned to a soldier.

40
00:02:32.320 --> 00:02:39.706
"Gather some soldiers and arrest the Tang Monk and his companions!"

41
00:02:39.707 --> 00:02:41.597
[g@"I'm glad we're headed west again,"

42
00:02:41.598 --> 00:02:45.379
said the Tang Monk as the travelers walked.@g]

43
00:02:45.380 --> 00:02:48.324
"I'm eager to reach the Western Paradise."

44
00:02:48.325 --> 00:02:49.720
[g@Wujing nodded.

45
00:02:49.721 --> 00:02:53.105
"We were delayed at Squire Kou's house for too long."@g]

46
00:02:53.106 --> 00:02:55.205
[g@Bajie snorted.

47
00:02:55.206 --> 00:02:58.338
"We should have stayed longer."@g]

48
00:02:58.339 --> 00:03:02.767
Suddenly a group of men stepped onto the road.

49
00:03:02.768 --> 00:03:05.875
[g@They carried swords and axes.

50
00:03:05.876 --> 00:03:09.269
Their horses carried several large bundles.@g]

51
00:03:09.270 --> 00:03:14.297
"Give us your money!" shouted one man.

52
00:03:14.298 --> 00:03:18.441
Wukong pulled out his iron bar.

53
00:03:18.442 --> 00:03:21.229
[g@"Wukong," said the Tang Monk.

54
00:03:21.230 --> 00:03:24.607
"Remember, you must not harm people."@g]

55
00:03:24.608 --> 00:03:26.343
[g@Wukong smiled.

56
00:03:26.344 --> 00:03:30.104
"I'm just going to talk to them, Master."@g]

57
00:03:30.105 --> 00:03:32.816
[g@He turned to the man who had shouted.

58
00:03:32.817 --> 00:03:35.315
"We have no money."@g]

59
00:03:35.316 --> 00:03:38.601
"No money, huh?" said the man.

60
00:03:38.602 --> 00:03:42.566
"Well then, we're going to beat up all of you."

61
00:03:42.567 --> 00:03:45.465
[g@Wukong laughed.

62
00:03:45.466 --> 00:03:47.988
"You don't realize who I am.

63
00:03:47.989 --> 00:03:52.141
I'm Sun Wukong, the Monkey King!"@g]

64
00:03:52.142 --> 00:03:55.593
"I don't care who you are," said the man.

65
00:03:55.594 --> 00:03:58.218
[g@"We're dangerous robbers!

66
00:03:58.219 --> 00:04:04.077
Last night we robbed a very wealthy squire."@g]

67
00:04:04.078 --> 00:04:08.573
The Tang Monk raised his eyebrows. "A squire?"

68
00:04:08.574 --> 00:04:14.030
Wukong quickly recited a spell, which froze the robbers.

69
00:04:14.031 --> 00:04:18.425
Wujing rushed to the horses and opened one of the bundles.

70
00:04:18.426 --> 00:04:23.149
Inside were dishes, jewels, and other valuable items.

71
00:04:23.150 --> 00:04:25.606
[g@Wujing gasped.

72
00:04:25.607 --> 00:04:28.324
"These items belong to Squire Kou!

73
00:04:28.325 --> 00:04:30.566
So do the horses!"@g]

74
00:04:30.567 --> 00:04:32.740
The Tang Monk bit his lip.

75
00:04:32.741 --> 00:04:35.071
[g@"Squire Kou is a good man.

76
00:04:35.072 --> 00:04:37.902
We must return his belongings."@g]

77
00:04:37.903 --> 00:04:40.544
[g@Everyone agreed.

78
00:04:40.545 --> 00:04:45.737
Wukong recited another spell, and the robbers became unfrozen.@g]

79
00:04:45.738 --> 00:04:50.255
The monkey grew large, and fire burned in his eyes.

80
00:04:50.256 --> 00:04:53.419
[g@"Get out of here!" he thundered.

81
00:04:53.420 --> 00:04:57.152
"And never steal again!"@g]

82
00:04:57.153 --> 00:05:02.699
The robbers screamed and ran away.

83
00:05:02.700 --> 00:05:06.965
The travelers headed back toward town with the squire's horses.

84
00:05:06.966 --> 00:05:11.291
Soon they saw a group of soldiers on horseback.

85
00:05:11.292 --> 00:05:14.771
"Those soldiers are riding toward us," said Wujing.

86
00:05:14.772 --> 00:05:17.724
"I wonder what they want," said the Tang Monk.

87
00:05:17.725 --> 00:05:21.764
One of the soldiers pointed a sword at the travelers.

88
00:05:21.765 --> 00:05:30.361
"Stop, thieves! You're all under arrest!"

